re he had fallen through space for more than sixteen miles and set a new world’s record for the free fall.\n\nDuring the 1960s, many young people liked to wear patches on their blue jeans and jackets.\nNo one knows how this fashion got started, but in the 1600s both men and women wore patches.\nPeople began to wear more and more patches—five, ten, fifteen, until they became so spotted that their faces were almost completely covered!\n"}}